<title>USA: Fed okay's Chinese bank bid to open office in U.S.</title>
<headline>Fed okay's Chinese bank bid to open office in U.S.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve Board said Wednesday it approved an application by Agriculture Bank of China to open a representative office in New York City.</p>
<p>The Beijing-based, government-owned bank is the second-largest of the four specialized banks in China with assets of $177 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The New York office would be used for marketing, research and liaison activities as well as certain loan solicitation and servicing activities, it said.</p>
